# Scripts here run on Linux. Never let a Windows checkout give them CRLF —
# a CR on the shebang line makes the kernel look for an interpreter that
# does not exist, and the failure ("bad interpreter") is deeply unhelpful.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer   text eol=lf
